thread:
maria: quick sync: propose a minimal adapter shim for continuous-batcher followup. goal: clear scheduler <-> adapter boundary so adapters can prefetch/warm without pulling scheduler internals.

alex: sounds good. main risks? leaks and revocation latency.

sara: prototype idea: 1) AcquireLease -> returns small Lease {id, deadline_ms, credit_est, warmup_token}. 2) Adapter can Reserve(lease_id) to materialize a microbatch, Release(lease_id) when done. 3) Revocations are server-streamed: Revoked(lease_id).

nina: add provisional-credit ledger: Acquire returns prov_id; adapter marks provisional credit in local store; Confirm(prov_id, final_cost) at dispatch reconciles. TTL and a reconciler avoid leaks.

tim: rollout: keep legacy path, feature-flag adapter-shim, start 5% traffic. add metrics: provisional_ttl_expired, revoked_missed_count, confirm_conflicts.

alex: proto sketch (compact):
```
message Lease { string id = 1; uint64 deadline_ms = 2; uint16 credit = 3; string warmup_token = 4; }
rpc Acquire(AcquireReq) returns (Lease);
rpc Reserve(ReserveReq) returns (Empty);
rpc Release(ReleaseReq) returns (Empty);
// server-stream Revoked { string lease_id }
rpc Confirm(ConfirmReq) returns (ConfirmResp); // atomic reconcile
```

maria: implementation notes: keep Lease tiny (ids + deadline). warmup_token references hotstore. Reconciler sweeps provisionals after TTL (default 5s). If adapter misses revoke, scheduler marks lease stale and dispatch ignores it.

sara: add debug verbose lease only via admin header. compact lease in prod.

infra-bot: NOTE: created issue #INF-2507 "adapter-shim-lease-and-ledger" (https://redwood/INF-2507)

maria: next: i'll draft RFC addendum with sequence diagrams and test plan (adapter crash, network partition, scheduler restart). ping me for review.

alex: i'll review reconcile path. thanks.
